.TH "SERVAL" "1" "Aug 2026" "Serval" "Serval Manual"

.SH NAME
serval-diff - Analyze the blast radius of changed files


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBserval diff [] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute impact for the set of recognized-module files changed between
 and the current working tree (including uncommitted changes).
Default  is HEAD, i.e. uncommitted changes only.

.PP
Each changed file gets its own report, and when at least two files are
analyzed, the whole change set is also scored as one: downstream impact
is deduplicated across the set, dependency edges between changed files
(interacting changes) and unchanged modules importing multiple changed
files (shared dependents) are surfaced separately, and CI relevance is
unioned. The set-level risk follows the same explainable rule-based
model as the per-file score.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--explain\fP[=false]
	ask an AI provider to explain each result's risk in natural language (one call per changed file — can be slow)

.PP
\fB--explain-host\fP=""
	Ollama host, --explain-provider=ollama only (default: $OLLAMA_HOST or http://localhost:11434)

.PP
\fB--explain-model\fP=""
	model to use (default: llama3.2 for ollama, the provider's own default otherwise)

.PP
\fB--explain-provider\fP="ollama"
	explain provider: ollama (local daemon), claude, codex, or gemini (local CLI, already authenticated)

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP=""
	exit with code 2 if risk is at or above this level (low, medium, high)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for diff

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	write the report to this file instead of stdout


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBserval(1)\fP


